WEBVTT

00:00:27.329 --> 00:00:30.121
In the short term, 
stress can be advantageous,

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:33.329
but when activated too often or too long,

00:00:33.371 --> 00:00:36.996
your primitive fight 
or flight stress response

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:39.121
not only changes your brain

00:00:39.162 --> 00:00:43.704
but also damages many of the other organs
and cells throughout your body.

00:00:44.787 --> 00:00:47.787
Your adrenal gland releases 
the stress hormones

00:00:47.829 --> 00:00:51.579
cortisol, epinephrine
also known as “adrenaline”,

00:00:51.621 --> 00:00:53.704
and norepinephrine.

00:00:53.746 --> 00:00:56.162
As these hormones travel 
through your bloodstream,

00:00:56.204 --> 00:00:59.037
they easily reach your blood 
vessels and heart.

00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:01.662
Adrenaline causes 
your heart to beat faster